# ORIN-DEFER (FBCONPAR item 2): UNAOS_ORINDEFER=1 arms `orindefer` — x86's PANEL-DEFER split
# layout/paint route, ported to the aarch64 console.
#
# THE GAP. `video/fbcon.rs::_print` runs its `PanelSink` route under `#[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]`,
# so every aarch64 console line falls to `print_masked`, which holds `without_interrupts` across the
# WHOLE line — layout AND every glyph's pixel writes. x86's own finding applies unchanged: only the
# LAYOUT half needs the mask (the lock is `try_lock`ed, and an IRQ-context printer reserves its own
# disjoint cells), so armed, layout stays masked and locked and the pixel work runs with interrupts
# enabled and no lock held.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS HERE BEYOND THE MASK SPAN: the wedge established 2026-08-26 runs `timer_preempt` ->
# `load_witness_emit` -> `serial_println!` -> `fbcon::_print` -> ... -> `wm::composite_inner` -> a bare
