    # [v3d103] VPMSTATIC line so no reader spends the boot on it either.
    # TWO CHANGES, BOTH INSTRUMENT-ONLY.
    # (1) THREE PCTR SLOTS RE-SOURCED. Slots 0/1/2/3/7 UNCHANGED — the five boot 13 read H4 off; leg H
    # must reproduce their shape or the line reads INCONCLUSIVE (an admissibility guard, not a result).
    # Slots 4/5/6 were L2T_VCD_READS + the two VPM STALL counters, all three of which read ZERO on boot
    # 13; VCD attribute fetch was already exonerated at PI-V3D-28, and a stall counter reading zero
    # cannot separate "the write sailed through" from "no write was ever presented". They become src33
    # QPU_CYCLES_STALLED_VERTEX_COORD_USER, src11 PTB_PRIM_CLIP and src10 PTB_PRIM_VIEWPOINT_DISCARD.
    # THE PAIR TO WATCH IS 5 AND 6: a primitive cannot be clipped or viewport-discarded unless it
    # ARRIVED, so either of them moving proves the VPM delivery reaches the PTB — which KILLS H4 and
    # moves the wall into the clipper/viewport room PI-V3D-17 opened.
    # (2) FOUR READ-ONLY REGISTERS JOIN THE READBACK SET: V3D_ERR_STAT, V3D_ERR_FDBGO, V3D_ERR_FDBGB,
    # V3D_ERR_FDBGS. Sourced from v3d_regs.h and scoped to THIS silicon by mainline itself —
    # v3d_debugfs.c's v3d_core_reg_defs lists all four as REGDEF(V3D_GEN_33, V3D_GEN_71, ...), a range
    # that brackets the bcm2711's V3D 4.2. Mainline's only use of them is a debugfs dump and this file
    # NEVER writes them. Twelve of ERR_STAT's sixteen named bits are VPM/VPA/VDW/VCD/VCM errors, which is
    # exactly the vocabulary the wall statement needs. Read PRISTINE once before leg E's kick and once
    # per armed leg; every row splits on NEWLY-LATCHED bits, because ERR_STAT latches and is never cleared.
    # Wire outcomes are pre-written on LEG H's own [v3d103] VPMPROBE VERDICT line:
    # V1 = a VPM WRITE bit latched (VPMEWNA "write non-allocated" or VPMEWR "write range") — THE VPM
    # WRITE IS REFUSED AND THE SILICON SAYS SO; the wall is ALLOCATION, and the three numbers that
    # allocate are cs_output_vpm_segment_size (this driver writes 1), cs_input_vpm_segment_size (0) and
    # VCM_CACHE_SIZE (4/4). V2 = a non-write VPM bit — the VPM is reached and unhappy, but not about our
    # stores. V3 = a VPA or VDW/VCD/VCM/L2C bit with NO VPM bit — the wall is BESIDE the VPM and the
    # §49.25.6 statement is misnamed. V4 = PTB_PRIM_CLIP and/or PTB_PRIM_VIEWPOINT_DISCARD moved — THE
    # PTB RECEIVED THE PRIMITIVES AND THREW THEM AWAY, and OUTCOME H4 IS DEAD. V5 = the coord thread
    # STALLED. V6 = nothing anywhere — THE WRITE IS SWALLOWED IN SILENCE, and the next rung must make the
    # thread's stores visible OUTSIDE the VPM (§49.25.7's TMU landmark). Three guards sit in front of all
    # six: an unarmed/flat-control bank, a leg H that did not reproduce boot 13's continuity slots, and a
    # frame that closed (which boot 13 says it will not).
    # NO register write, NO mailbox tag and NO page-table edit is added over UNAOS_V3D_HFIRST.
    # ⚠ an armed boot deliberately produces a SHORT capture missing every banked witness: label it and
    # NEVER diff it line-for-line against a full deep boot. QEMU raspi4b models no V3D at all, so
    # [v3d95] prints its hub-absent SKIPPED line and returns before any leg is reached — kernel8-test
    # green means no regression and nothing more; the verdict is attended metal.
    if [ -n "${UNAOS_V3D_VPMPROBE:-}" ]; then
        K8_FEATS="${K8_FEATS},v3d_vpmprobe,v3d_hfirst,v3d_dispatchdisc,v3d_bincontent,v3d_armedclose,v3d_tsaim,v3d_basedaim,v3d_unarmclose,v3d"
        echo -e "${COLOR_YELLOW}  • UNAOS_V3D_VPMPROBE: the [v3d103] vpmprobe discriminator rung — NO new leg, NO new kick, NO new shader word and NO new register WRITE; it re-sources PCTR slots 4/5/6 to QPU_CYCLES_STALLED_VERTEX_COORD_USER / PTB_PRIM_CLIP / PTB_PRIM_VIEWPOINT_DISCARD (leaving the five slots boot 13 read OUTCOME H4 off untouched as an admissibility guard) and adds four READ-ONLY error registers (V3D_ERR_STAT/FDBGO/FDBGB/FDBGS, scoped to this silicon by mainline's own v3d_core_reg_defs), with §49.25.7's V1..V6 outcomes pre-written on leg H's own verdict line (⚠ implies UNAOS_V3D_HFIRST; short capture — do not diff against a deep boot)${COLOR_RESET}"
